# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: at sync (obj.x.changed?) — synchronous slot-change subscriber;
#         body runs inline before the slot-write statement returns; value
#         visible to subscriber is the new value just written.
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Activation history: Cat. E re-audit Cluster #15 verdict A reclassified
# the original `at.sync` dot-syntax as a fixture-authoring error
# (urbiscript has no dot-syntax for sync watchers; the canonical form is
# the `at sync (cond) body` keyword phrase shipped at M5 per §S-watcher-3
# — see at_sync_no_yield.chk).  Rewritten to keyword form + attempted
# activation at v0.10.12.
#
# blocked: slot-change fires on first slot-install as well as write
#          (double-fire bug, same as slot_change_basic.chk) — v1.0-rc
#          investigation.  The `at sync` keyword form is correct per
#          §S-watcher-3; the remaining blocker is the scripted slot-change
#          subscriber wiring, not the sync-watcher syntax.
#
# Reason:
#   Same blockers as slot_change_basic.chk.  The sync (AT_SYNC) vs async (AT)
#   mode distinction for slot-change watchers is documented in spec #4 §5.3 and
#   tested in test_slot_change_reentrancy.c at the C level.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate when slot-change double-fire bug resolved):
#   var obj = Object.new();
#   var Realm.seen = 0;
#   at sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.seen = obj.x;
#   obj.x = 7;
#   Realm.seen
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 7
